{
  "about": "Param descriptors shared by the two twins of the param schema: arsenal/web/lib/params.js (tests/params_schema.test.mjs) and arsenal/params.py (tests/test_params_schema.py). The verdicts both must reproduce are in verdicts.json beside this file. Descriptors here may leave optional fields out (curve, help, recBlocked, order, uniform, derived, cost); the schema fills them. The headers are written for this fixture in our own words: aurora-sheets is the example recipe header of the unified architecture draft (section 3.2), display-out is the house display seam of atlas H9, twin-demo exercises a derived param, a colour, a vector and a toggle. The edge set holds a step below a millionth, a range past 2^53 and a choice worth 2^60; the deep set holds derived expressions at, over and far over the 128-token cap; the tiny set holds ranges without a step whose ends need more than six decimals (one of them more than nine). No corpus code anywhere.",
